    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.25,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.15,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.22 from 6 h to 18 h, which could mean reader saturation. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test this. The 10x dilution read 0.1325, which scales to 1.33. The 25x dilution read 0.0482, which scales to 1.21. The undiluted 18 h reading was 1.209. The two scaled values do not agree with each other, and only the 10x value is above the undiluted reading. The 25x value matches it almost exactly. If the reader were saturating, the scaled dilution values would be clearly higher than the undiluted reading and would rise with dilution. They do not. Each dilution has only one replicate, so the 10x result is probably noise of around 9%. The plateau looks like true stationary phase, with biomass about 1.2 to 1.3 OD."
  },
